    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d680">

                <pb facs="0740" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/73: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-27T18:00:00+08:00">March 27, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 27—6:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>381. 1. Following from American Consul General at Mukden.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“March 27, 9 a.m. The new Chinese Mayor of Mukden, appointed by Provincial
                        Government, has invited consular corps and staffs to dinner at Yamato Hotel
                        on March 29th. My British colleague has accepted while some others are
                        undecided. Unless Legation disapproves my staff will accept. I am having
                        another engagement. Request immediate instructions.”</p></quote>
                <p>2. Myers is being informed neither he nor members of consular staff should accept
                    such invitation unless with the Department’s express approval. Please instruct
                    Mukden direct.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d680-f1"/></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d680-f1" n="32" xml:id="d680-f1-content">
                <p>The Department instructed the Consul General at Mukden in telegram of March 27, 1
                    p.m.: “Department approves your plan: your staff accept, you decline.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
